module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.EmbeddedResolution.CartierDescent.ChartIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.EmbeddedResolution.CartierDescent.TwoChartCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafComapMul

/-!
# The two charts of the blowup of a regular local surface at its closed point

Let `A` be a two-dimensional regular local ring with maximal ideal `𝔪 = (x, y)`. This file is the
dictionary between ideal-theoretic computations in the affine blowup algebras `A[𝔪/x]` and
`A[𝔪/y]` and statements about ideal sheaves on the blowup `X` of `Spec A` at its closed point.

The blowup is spelled `blowUp (centre A)`, where `centre A` is the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf
attached to the maximal ideal through the canonical ring isomorphism
`ι : A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`; this is the spelling used by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_blowUp_maximalIdeal`. More generally `idealSheafOf A L` is the ideal
sheaf attached to an ideal `L` of `A`. On the only affine open that matters — all of
`Spec A` — the sections of `idealSheafOf A L` are `L·Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`, so the sections of the centre
are generated by `ι x` and `ι y`.

Three things are then proved. The two charts `Spec A[𝔪/x]` and `Spec A[𝔪/y]` cover the whole
blowup, not merely the part over an affine open, because `Spec A` is itself affine: this is the
second assertion of Stacks tag 0804, cut down to a two-element generating family by
`Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart_pair`. On such a chart the inverse image
`L·𝒪_X` of `idealSheafOf A L` is the extension of `L` along `A ⟶ Γ(Spec A, ⊤) ⟶ A[𝔪/a]`. And on
the same chart the exceptional ideal is generated by the image of `a`, so its `d`-th power — the
ideal sheaf `𝒪_X(-dE)` — is generated by the image of `a ^ d`.

Together these are the bookkeeping behind Stacks tag 0AGT: they turn the colength computations in
`A[𝔪/x]` and `A[𝔪/y]` into the comparison of `L·𝒪_X` with `𝒪_X(-dE)` on the blowup.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.centre` and
  `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.idealSheafOf`: the blowup centre and, more
  generally, the ideal sheaf on `Spec A` attached to an ideal of `A`.
* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.idealSheafOf_ideal_top` and
  `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.centre_ideal_top_eq_map`: their sections over all
  of `Spec A`.
* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.centre_ideal_top`: for `𝔪 = (x, y)` the sections of
  the centre over all of `Spec A` are generated by `ι x` and `ι y`, with
  `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_centre_ideal_top_x` and
  `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_centre_ideal_top_y` the two memberships that
  name the charts.
* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_opensRange_chart_or`: the charts of `ι x` and
  `ι y` cover the blowup.
* `CartierDescent.ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span` and
  `CartierDescent.ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_pow_eq_span`: over an arbitrary
  base, the exceptional ideal of a blowup read on the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` is generated
  by the image of `a`, and its `d`-th power by the image of `a ^ d`.
* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.ideal_comap_chart_eq_map`: the inverse image of
  `idealSheafOf A L` read on the chart of `a` is `L·A[𝔪/a]`.
* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal` and
  `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal_pow`: the two
  preceding results for the surface blowup, where the base is `Spec A` and the chart is the one
  of `ι x` or of `ι y`.

## Implementation notes

`centre` and `idealSheafOf` carry only `[CommRing A]` and `[IsLocalRing A]`; neither regularity
nor the dimension hypothesis is used anywhere in this file. Two generators of `𝔪` are *assumed*,
as `hspan : Ideal.span {x, y} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A`, which is what a two-dimensional
regular local ring supplies and what the statements actually need. `centre A` is by definition
`idealSheafOf A (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)`, and both unfold to the literal spelling
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.map ι 𝔪)` used in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/RegularSurfaceBlowup.lean`, so a consumer may pass either
form to the results proved there.

The blowup and its exceptional ideal are spelled `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp` and
`Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal` throughout, not the `AlgebraicGeometry` abbreviations of the
same names: `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart` is a morphism into the former, so the charts and
the ideal sheaves compared with them must live over the same scheme.

The affine open of `Spec A` is written out as the anonymous constructor
`⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩` rather than abbreviated, so that `Γ(Spec A, _)` in the type of the
chart generator `a` stays syntactically `Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)`.

Both chart computations keep the generator `a` as a parameter, so a caller instantiates at `ι x`
or at `ι y` with `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_centre_ideal_top_x` or
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_centre_ideal_top_y`; there is no asymmetry
between the two charts to record.

Each is proved over an arbitrary base first and then instantiated at `centre A`, and that split
is forced rather than stylistic. The heartbeat budget is per declaration, and in this area it is
spent on unfolding `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp` and `affineBlowup`; a single `rw` whose rewrite rule
must be matched against a goal mentioning *both* the blowup of `centre A` and an `Ideal.map`
through `Γ(Spec ·, ⊤)` exhausts it. So the pattern of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ExceptionalChart.lean` is followed throughout: the purely
ring-theoretic steps are isolated behind variables (`Ideal.map_pow`, `Ideal.map_map`,
`map_hom_span_singleton_inv`), the commutation of powers with inverse image and with reading on
an affine open is isolated with both schemes behind variables (`ideal_comap_pow_top`), and the
results are then composed with `congrArg` and `Eq.trans` against lemmas whose types are
inferred — never by `rw` on the assembled statement.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CommRingCat

universe u

namespace Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]

/-! ### The centre of the blowup -/

/-- **The ideal sheaf on `Spec A` attached to an ideal of `A`.** The quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals whose sections over all of `Spec A` are the extension of `L` along the canonical ring
isomorphism `ι : A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`. -/
public def idealSheafOf (L : Ideal A) : (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
    (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom L)

/-- **The centre of the blowup of `Spec A` at its closed point.** The quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals attached to the maximal ideal of a local ring `A`; blowing it up is the spelling of "the
blowup of `Spec A` at its closed point" used by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_blowUp_maximalIdeal`. -/
public def centre : (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
    (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))

/-- The centre of the blowup is the ideal sheaf attached to the maximal ideal. -/
public theorem centre_eq_idealSheafOf :
    centre A = idealSheafOf A (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) := rfl

/-- **The sections of `idealSheafOf A L` over all of `Spec A`.** They form the extension of `L`
along `ι : A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`. -/
public theorem idealSheafOf_ideal_top (L : Ideal A) :
    (idealSheafOf A L).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom L := by
  simp [idealSheafOf]

/-- **The sections of the blowup centre over all of `Spec A`.** They form the extension of the
maximal ideal along `ι : A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`. -/
public theorem centre_ideal_top_eq_map :
    (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :=
  idealSheafOf_ideal_top A (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)

variable {A} in
/-- An element of the maximal ideal gives a section of the blowup centre over all of
`Spec A`. -/
public theorem mem_centre_ideal_top {a : A} (ha : a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom a ∈
      (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ :=
  (centre_ideal_top_eq_map A).symm ▸ Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

/-- **The blowup centre of a two-generated maximal ideal.** If `𝔪 = (x, y)` then the sections of
the centre over all of `Spec A` are generated by `ι x` and `ι y`. -/
public theorem centre_ideal_top (x y : A)
    (hspan : Ideal.span {x, y} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom x,
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom y} := by
  rw [centre_ideal_top_eq_map, ← hspan, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_pair]

variable {A} in
/-- The first of two generators of the maximal ideal gives a section of the blowup centre over
all of `Spec A`; this is what names the `x`-chart of the blowup. -/
public theorem mem_centre_ideal_top_x {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span {x, y} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom x ∈
      (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ :=
  mem_centre_ideal_top (hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert _ _))

variable {A} in
/-- The second of two generators of the maximal ideal gives a section of the blowup centre over
all of `Spec A`; this is what names the `y`-chart of the blowup. -/
public theorem mem_centre_ideal_top_y {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span {x, y} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom y ∈
      (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ :=
  mem_centre_ideal_top (hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ rfl))

/-! ### The two charts cover the blowup -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0804, second assertion, for the blowup of a local ring at its closed
point.** If the maximal ideal of `A` is generated by `x` and `y`, then every point of the blowup
of `Spec A` at its closed point lies on the chart `Spec A[𝔪/x]` or on the chart `Spec A[𝔪/y]`.

The cover is over the whole blowup, not merely over an affine open of the base, because the base
`Spec A` is itself affine, so the open `⊤` on which the centre is two-generated is all of it. -/
public theorem mem_opensRange_chart_or (x y : A)
    (hspan : Ideal.span {x, y} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (z : Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)) :
    z ∈ (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
        (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan)).opensRange ∨
      z ∈ (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
        (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan)).opensRange :=
  Stacks.Blowup.mem_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart_pair (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
    (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan) (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan)
    (centre_ideal_top A x y hspan) z trivial

/-! ### The exceptional ideal on a chart, over an arbitrary base -/

/-- Mapping a principal ideal generated by the image of `t` under the inverse of a ring
isomorphism forward along that isomorphism gives the ideal generated by `t`. -/
private theorem map_hom_span_singleton_inv {R T : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : R ≅ T) (t : T) :
    Ideal.map e.hom.hom (Ideal.span {e.inv.hom t}) = Ideal.span {t} := by
  have ht : e.hom.hom (e.inv.hom t) = t := congrArg (fun φ : T ⟶ T => φ.hom t) e.inv_hom_id
  rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, ht]

/-- **The sections of a power of an inverse-image ideal sheaf over an affine target.** Inverse
image commutes with powers of ideal sheaves (`Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_pow`), and so does reading
an ideal sheaf on an affine open (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow`).

Both schemes are behind variables so that neither the blowup nor the spectrum of an affine blowup
algebra has to be unfolded while this step is checked. -/
private theorem ideal_comap_pow_top {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] (Z : X.IdealSheafData)
    (f : Y ⟶ X) (d : ℕ) :
    ((Z ^ d).comap f).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      (Z.comap f).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ^ d :=
  (congrArg (fun K : Y.IdealSheafData => K.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩)
      (Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_pow Z f d)).trans
    (congrFun (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow (I := Z.comap f) d) _)

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (ℐ : S.IdealSheafData) (U : S.affineOpens)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS, on an affine chart of a blowup, as an ideal of the affine blowup
algebra.** Transporting the sections of the exceptional ideal over the chart
`Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` along the canonical identification of those sections with
`Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` gives the principal ideal generated by the image of `a`.

This is `Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart` in the form in which
consumers want it, exactly as
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_top_eq_map` is the
consumable form of the computation for a general ideal sheaf. -/
public theorem ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span {a : Γ(S, U.1)}
    (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).hom.hom
        (((Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal ℐ).comap
          (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a) a} := by
  rw [Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart,
    map_hom_span_singleton_inv]

/-- **The `d`-th power of the exceptional ideal on an affine chart of a blowup.** Transporting
the sections of `(ℐ·𝒪_{X'})^d` over the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` along the canonical
identification of those sections with `Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` gives the principal ideal generated by
the image of `a ^ d`.

Inverse image and reading on an affine open both commute with powers
(the private `ideal_comap_pow_top` above), so this is
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span`
raised to the `d`-th power. -/
public theorem ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_pow_eq_span {a : Γ(S, U.1)}
    (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) (d : ℕ) :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).hom.hom
        (((Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal ℐ ^ d).comap
          (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a) a ^ d} := by
  have h2 := congrArg (fun J => Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso
    (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).hom.hom J)
    (ideal_comap_pow_top (Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal ℐ)
      (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha) d)
  have h3 := congrArg (fun J => J ^ d)
    (ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span ℐ U ha)
  exact h2.trans ((Ideal.map_pow _ _ d).trans (h3.trans (Ideal.span_singleton_pow _ d)))

/-! ### Ideal sheaves read on a chart of the surface blowup -/

/-- **The inverse image of `idealSheafOf A L` read on a chart of the blowup.** On the chart
`Spec A[𝔪/a]` attached to a section `a` of the centre, the ideal of `L·𝒪_X` is the extension of
`L` along the composite `A ⟶ Γ(Spec A, ⊤) ⟶ A[𝔪/a]`.

This is the local computation `L·A[𝔪/a]` that the colength bookkeeping of Stacks tag 0AGT runs
in; the caller instantiates `a` at `ι x` or at `ι y` through
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_centre_ideal_top_x` or
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_centre_ideal_top_y`. -/
public theorem ideal_comap_chart_eq_map (L : Ideal A)
    {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
        ((((idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A))).comap
          (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.map ((algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a)).comp
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom) L := by
  have h := ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_top_eq_map (centre A) (idealSheafOf A L)
    ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha
  have h2 := congrArg (fun J => Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
    (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a)) J) (idealSheafOf_ideal_top A L)
  exact h.trans (h2.trans (Ideal.map_map (I := L) _ _))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS, on a chart of the blowup of a local ring at its closed point.**
On the chart `Spec A[𝔪/a]` attached to a section `a` of the centre, the exceptional ideal is
generated by the image of `a`. -/
public theorem ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
        (((Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A)).comap
          (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
                    (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a} :=
  ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span (centre A)
    ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha

/-- **The `d`-th power of the exceptional ideal read on a chart of the blowup.** On the chart
`Spec A[𝔪/a]` attached to a section `a` of the centre, the ideal sheaf `𝒪_X(-dE)` is generated by
the image of `a ^ d`.

This is the right-hand side of the comparison `L·𝒪_X = 𝒪_X(-dE)·L'` that Stacks tag 0AGT
computes with. -/
public theorem ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal_pow {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) (d : ℕ) :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
        (((Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d).comap
          (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
                    (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ^ d} :=
  ideal_comap_blowUpAffineChart_exceptionalIdeal_pow_eq_span (centre A)
    ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha d

end Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent

end
